  "unique_standalone_prefix": "\\documentclass[11pt]{article}\n\\usepackage{iftex}\n\\ifPDFTeX\n\\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}\n\\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}\n\\else\n\\usepackage{fontspec}\n\\fi\n\\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb}\n\\usepackage[margin=1in]{geometry}\n\\usepackage{fancyvrb}\n\\usepackage[hidelinks]{hyperref}\n\\DefineVerbatimEnvironment{QualifiedInput}{Verbatim}{fontsize=\\tiny}\n\\setlength{\\parindent}{0pt}\n\\setlength{\\parskip}{0.5em}\n\\emergencystretch=4em\n\\title{Corrected formal envelopes and a toric obstacle sector\\\\\nWhole-proof audit and a normal nonisolated correction obstruction}\n\\author{Independent local reconstruction; unverified mathematical draft}\n\\date{9 October 2026}\n\\begin{document}\n\\maketitle\n\\begin{abstract}\nWe audit the entire corrected formal BIG and isolated envelope theorem,\nexplicitly reject the immutable root-scalar error, and reconstruct its repair.\nWe prove geometrically positive continuous envelopes for every continuous\nmonomial-weight obstacle on complete normal toric germs over any field.\nRational signed monomial obstacles have actual primary-ideal envelopes\ncomputed by a finite rational polyhedron. An independently proved all-map\ntest-ideal formula on a normal nonisolated threefold rules out one universal\nprimary subadditivity correction. It does not contradict envelope continuity.\nThe unchanged general original P12.3 remains incomplete. Candidate=false.\nThis is standalone source, deliberately uncompiled for ROOT.\n\\end{abstract}\n\\tableofcontents\n\\newpage\n",
